   "widgets_values": [
    "A weathered brass compass resting on a folded nautical chart in a lighthouse keeper's study, late afternoon light raking across the desk through a salt streaked window. The chart shows hand inked coastlines, depth soundings and a pencilled course line; a small card tucked under the compass rim reads \"TRUE NORTH\" in crisp letterpress capitals. Beside it sit a stub of red wax, a coil of tarred twine and a chipped enamel mug. Warm amber light against cool teal shadow, fine grain in the aged paper, tarnish and fingerprints on the brass, shallow depth of field with the far edge of the desk softening into haze. Photographic realism, 2K detail, natural colour."
